prompt:
`cssVar(name, fallback)` returns a `var()` reference. Custom property names must start with `--`;
callers sometimes pass `"brand"` and sometimes `"--brand"`. Add the fallback only when one is given:
`cssVar("brand", "#333")` → `"var(--brand, #333)"`.

coding.referenceSolution:
function cssVar(name, fallback) {
  const prop = name.startsWith("--") ? name : `--${name}`;
  return fallback === undefined || fallback === null ? `var(${prop})` : `var(${prop}, ${fallback})`;
}

